  "diagnostic_status": "NO_SUPPORT_FOR_SIMPLE_STATE_STALENESS_PATTERN",
  "claim_boundary": [
    "Durif stage is measured only at capture; no individual is re-staged at activation.",
    "Latency is itself a post-capture movement outcome and is not randomized.",
    "This analysis can weaken or support a state-staleness explanation but cannot prove physiological convergence.",
    "Thresholds of 1, 3 and 7 days are fixed before running this diagnostic and must all be reported."
  ],
  "diagnostic_interpretation": "The simple state-staleness prediction is not supported: the Durif x log-latency interaction is not negative, and stage-speed point estimates remain near or below 1 among eels activating within 1, 3, or 7 days. Moderate short-latency effects cannot be ruled out because intervals are wide, and no individual was re-staged."
}
